@CareRoute.Api_HostAddress = http://localhost:7015

### List all patients → expect 200 with 3 items
GET {{CareRoute.Api_HostAddress}}/api/patients
Accept: application/json

### One existing patient (Lotte Peeters) → expect 200
GET {{CareRoute.Api_HostAddress}}/api/patients/3f2c1a9e-6b1d-4c7a-9a51-0f4e2b7d8c11
Accept: application/json
###

### T3 — Unknown but well-formed id → expect 404 WITH a ProblemDetails body
GET {{CareRoute.Api_HostAddress}}/api/patients/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001
Accept: application/json

### T4 — Malformed id (not a GUID) → expect 404 with an EMPTY body
GET {{CareRoute.Api_HostAddress}}/api/patients/not-a-guid
Accept: application/json

### T5 — Routing is case-insensitive → expect 200 with 3 items
GET {{CareRoute.Api_HostAddress}}/API/Patients
Accept: application/json

### T6 — Unsupported method → expect 405 Method Not Allowed
DELETE {{CareRoute.Api_HostAddress}}/api/patients/3f2c1a9e-6b1d-4c7a-9a51-0f4e2b7d8c11

### T7 — register a patient (expect 201 + Location)
POST {{CareRoute.Api_HostAddress}}/api/patients
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Noor",
  "lastName": "Janssens",
  "dateOfBirth": "1990-05-12"
}

### T8 — health (expect 200 Healthy)
GET {{CareRoute.Api_HostAddress}}/health

### T9 — missing firstName (expect 400 ValidationProblemDetails, errors.FirstName)
POST {{CareRoute.Api_HostAddress}}/api/patients
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "lastName": "Maes",
  "dateOfBirth": "1990-05-12"
}

### T10 — missing dateOfBirth (expect 400, errors.DateOfBirth)
POST {{CareRoute.Api_HostAddress}}/api/patients
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Noor",
  "lastName": "Janssens"
}

### T11 — firstName exactly 100 chars (expect 201)
POST {{CareRoute.Api_HostAddress}}/api/patients
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa",
  "lastName": "Boundary",
  "dateOfBirth": "1990-05-12"
}

### T12 — firstName 101 chars (expect 400, errors.FirstName)
POST {{CareRoute.Api_HostAddress}}/api/patients
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa",
  "lastName": "Boundary",
  "dateOfBirth": "1990-05-12"
}

### T13 — client sends its own id (expect 201 with a DIFFERENT, server-generated id)
# @name overpost
POST {{CareRoute.Api_HostAddress}}/api/patients
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "id": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001",
  "firstName": "Sofie",
  "lastName": "Wouters",
  "dateOfBirth": "1978-09-03"
}

### T13b — the created patient is reachable at its new id (expect 200)
GET {{CareRoute.Api_HostAddress}}/api/patients/{{overpost.response.body.$.id}}

### T14 — deliberate exception (expect 500 ProblemDetails, no stack trace, no exception message)
GET {{CareRoute.Api_HostAddress}}/api/diagnostics/throw

### T15 — unknown patient (expect 404 ProblemDetails with "title": "Not Found")
GET {{CareRoute.Api_HostAddress}}/api/patients/11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111